bound-lock/1 about="Under uniform truth and an independent covering-cause indicator of mass c, active observations copy one n-ary symmetric channel of accuracy q; I(truth;observations) <= log2(n)-c*(h(q)+(1-q)*log2(n-1)); copies add no information. Historical alias: reliability-is-encounter-rate. No achievability or partial governance claim." at=witness:042/joint-capacity-confidence by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/measures/t12/common-cause.json|vectors/measures/t12/expected.json role=demands scope=law/T12-reliability-is-encounter-rate value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="In a common probability space with justified declared failure upper bounds p_i, the probability of all declared events succeeding is at least max(0,1-sum(p_i)); sum(p_i)>=1 is trivial. Agreement and copy counts do not estimate probabilities. Historical alias: freedom-is-a-currency; no transferability or unforgeability claim." at=witness:042/joint-capacity-confidence by=target form=alphabet kind=theorem measure=status needs=samples/measures/confidence/union-bound.json|vectors/measures/confidence/expected.json role=demands scope=law/T18-freedom-is-a-currency value=present view=valuation
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=test/t38-forms.test.ts|vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json|vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json role=writes scope=obligations/theory/T38 value="For closed real intervals, pairwise nonempty intersections suffice for finite families; this is not a claim about every lattice form. Convex sets in R^d require the hypotheses of Helly and witnesses up to d+1. A three-arc discrete circle and fixed halfplanes distinguish two- and three-member empty meets."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/t38/circle12.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F2 value="On twelve discrete points, five-point arcs starting at 0, 4 and 8 meet in every pair and not jointly. This finite example does not prove the absence of every finite Helly bound."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/t38/halfplanes.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F3 value="The four seller/buyer/carrier/auditor halfplanes conflict with seller/auditor witness; x>=0,y>=0,x+y<=-1 is pairwise consistent and jointly empty. Fixed nonnegative certificates verify these finite cases only."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/t87/phase-controls.json|samples/laws/t87/phase-domain.json|test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F4 value="Under the provisional integer domain p divides n and 0<=s<p, RI=log2(n/p)-h(s/p). For n=12,p=4, the controls at s=0,1,2,3 are 1.584962500721156,0.7736843762620231,0.5849625007211561,0.7736843762620231 bits. Halfphase is one bit below inphase. Author domain confirmation and worst-case objective remain open."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=test/measures/t87-phase.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/T87 value="The raw absolute-angle criterion is not invariant under adding a full turn: phases 0 and 2pi reinforce. Existing cancels uses cos of the difference. This distinguishes a missing wrapped-distance hypothesis; it does not infer laminarity or a near-phase RI worst-case objective."
bound-lock/1 about="Unsigned proposed research statement; native reader capture and admitted closure pending." at=witness:042/joint-forms-phase by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=vectors/laws/f1/finite-arithmetic.json|test/t38-forms.test.ts role=writes scope=obligations/theory/F1 value="For n=3..7, arithmetic reproduces the provided log2(n)-2+2/n values and Bell squared pair counts. No exhaustive partition enumeration, general optimality proof or independent browser/WebAssembly-origin verification was performed."
bound-lock/1 about="stated as a hint and never as a claim about the world: if what is is a field of floors and ceilings, a distant signature changes a cell whose own record never moved, and in two hundred trials of one cell holding one value the verdict came out both ways, so nothing stored at the cell explains the difference and what explains it is the bound the cell rests on; the resemblance is structural and never arithmetic, with no continuous amplitudes and no inequality violated by number; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=witness:042/relabel-observations by=target form=alphabet kind=experiment measure=status needs=samples/yes/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json|samples/no/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move.json restsOn=law/T46-a-bound-moves-cells-no-walk-reaches|law/T47-a-two-pole-object role=demands scope=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="amplitudes with a phase and no origin, no signed ceiling, no resolution and no epoch band are what is left of a cell when those four fields are dropped, so the measurement problem is the absence of who, imposed symmetries the absence of a signed ceiling, the classical limit the absence of resolution and universal interference the absence of bands; restored, four claims in phase keep exactly the share of the whole their number leaves them against an environment spread over the period, and six origins around one value are six objects read finely and one read coarsely, so how many things there are is a reading; structural resemblance, one origin, not a claim about the world" at=witness:042/relabel-observations by=target form=alphabet kind=experiment measure=status needs=samples/yes/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json|samples/no/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields.json restsOn=law/H3-a-distant-signature-moves-a-cell-that-did-not-move|law/T49-amplitude-has-sign-and-phase|law/T36-agreement-has-a-resolution|law/T45-cells-that-rest-on-one-bound-are-entangled role=demands scope=law/H5-hilbert-is-the-obligatory-without-four-fields value=present view=lattice
bound-lock/1 about="Folding claims is union in the knowledge order; arrival order never decides." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L1 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="For intervals of a lattice, pairs suffice: every conflict has a witness of two (Helly number 2). Convex forms in\n   R^d need witnesses up to d+1 (d=2 → 3). Cyclic forms (phase) without a declared cut have no finite Helly number;\n   with a declared cut, h=2 on arcs not crossing it. Shannon partitions have no finite Helly number." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L2 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Excluding any value from the maximal coincidence may exclude the truth; keeping the fork is the only correct action." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L3 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Each entering origin closes bits and spends confidence; the guarantee of the meet is 1 − Σp UNDER DECLARED,\n   JUSTIFIED failure probabilities p_i; if Σp ≥ 1 the bound is trivial and must be reported as such. Agreement\n   and copy count do not estimate p." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L4 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="In the Shannon lattice, shared information may have no carrier: at most log₂n − 2 + 2/n bits." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L5 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Information about the truth is bounded by the structure of causes, not by the number of witnesses; copies do not add." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L6 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="A closed group cannot measure its own reliability: for a cause covering all witnesses, P(unanimity on v) = c/n\n   for every accuracy q, so q is unidentifiable from inside." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L7 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Only dissent identifies what origins share; unanimity says nothing. For a partial cause, q is identified iff an\n   outsider exists with error p ≠ (n−1)/n. Rank-breaking structures: same-set factors, singleton factors,\n   cycle-covering factors, more factors than pairs." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L8 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Which parameters can be measured is known before observing, from the pairs matrix of declared causes." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/L9 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Extremal: over n equiprobable states, max RI(x,y) = log₂n − 2 + 2/n, attained only by the path on n+1 vertices\n   (x groups edges by even endpoint, y by odd). Proof chain: lem-phi (φ(t) ≥ 2(t−1)) → lem-merge → lem-identity →\n   lem-join → lem-meet → thm-extremal. Enumeration n=3..7: 0.251629, 0.500000, 0.721928, 0.918296, 1.093069;\n   pair counts 25, 225, 2704, 41209, 769129 (Bell numbers squared → complete)." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F1 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Circle of 12 points, arcs of length 5 starting at 0, 4, 8: every pair meets, the three do not." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F2 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Half-plane claims x+y≤12 (seller), x≥3 (buyer), y≥2 (carrier), x+y≥14 (auditor): CONFLICT, witness\n   {seller, auditor}, 2 of 4. Minimal example needing three: x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0, x + y ≤ −1 (pairwise consistent,\n   jointly empty). Both go in as vectors." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F3 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Phase: RI = log₂(n/p) − h(s/p) with n states, period p dividing n, shift s with 0 ≤ s < p, h the binary entropy;\n   worst case is near-phase, not anti-phase. (Author to confirm the domain; until then the vector carries these\n   hypotheses explicitly.)" at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F4 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="M/4: with a common cause c of accuracy q, C = log₂n − c·[h(q) + (1−q)·log₂(n−1)]; dissent\n   d = (1−c)·[1 − (1−p)² − p²/(n−1)]. Sample n=4, c=1/5: one covering factor q=0 → 1.683 bits; {A,B},{A,B} → 1.430;\n   {A,B},{C,D} → 1.937; triangle {A,B},{B,C},{A,C} → 1.835; q=1/2 → 1.642. Numeric policy: binary64-log2.\n   Negative sample (each a named refusal): missing q → refuse; 2 witnesses requesting c → unmeasured; 3 binary\n   witnesses → unmeasured; perfect agreement → no-dissent; copies → same bound; partial governance → unmeasured.\n   HOW FACTORS GOVERN in duplicated/disjoint/triangle models is NOT fully specified: region stays open (§5)." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/F5 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Obligations: a cell may declare names it needs; an obligation is an open region of form bytes inside the cell\n   (not an edge). Bytes hashing to the name narrow it to a point; received bytes are themselves a cell whose open\n   regions fold inside the parent's. Terminates: the knowledge order is well-founded, plus an instruction budget." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P1 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Byte regions: open / resolved / fork (two holders, two byte sets: both kept) / unmet (no holder: stop, name it).\n   Wrong bytes are refused, never patched." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P2 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Named core: a result declares the names it depends on; validity is a function of that core only." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P3 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Root as a cell of names: a list of names folds into one name. Atoms (form bytes) have no dissent; dissent lives\n   in claims. The atom zero (fold/hash/assemble) is trusted out of band; in Bound it is the WebAssembly kernel." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P4 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Name in the fragment: a link carries #form:hash, not a place; the form is in the name because it declares how\n   claims combine (Helly order). Expected addresses: hash(\"answer to claim X\") is known before the answer exists." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P5 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Paper as holder: a QR holds a name or small bytes (one QR 2,953 B; A4 sheet ≈140 KB); two tiers of \"belongs to\n   no one\": complete-on-paper, and named (bytes exist while someone keeps them)." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P6 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Copresence: commit-reveal; horizon ≥ max latency; decisions with duration; actions as intervals." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P7 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Fold-as-you-go: resolve by frontier, by need, by proximity." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P8 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Universality test: a primitive enters only if it means the same in a game, a news story and a sensor without\n   code change. Never in a contract: ticks, demos, games, pages, APIs." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P9 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Derived regions: form=derived, value = f(named regions), closing policy eager|deferred (from Scion's derived\n   data; passes P9). Verification is a claim, not a gate: implementation claims fold immediately; verification is\n   a derived region closed later. Cost of folding a cell ∝ the cell, never the world." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md role=writes scope=theory/source/P10 value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="Verbatim declared theory prose through the already selected text producer; no proof or computed research status is asserted." at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=id needs=docs/theory.lines role=demands scope=view/theory shape=docs/theory.md value=text
bound-lock/1 about="# Obligations 0.4.2 — theory under review\n\nThese are proposed author statements from the historical source docs/theory-2026-10.md. Research status is OPEN: proof chains, independent origins and native distinguishing vectors have not been admitted or paid by this preparation. The historical source’s attribution of two independent origins is preserved as author text only; it is not a verified-2-origins claim here. Numeric examples establish no general theorem. Mixed statements, factor governance, F4 objective/domain and L7 interpretation remain open.\n\n## L1 — OPEN author statement\n\nFolding claims is union in the knowledge order; arrival order never decides.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L2 — OPEN author statement\n\nFor intervals of a lattice, pairs suffice: every conflict has a witness of two (Helly number 2). Convex forms in\n   R^d need witnesses up to d+1 (d=2 → 3). Cyclic forms (phase) without a declared cut have no finite Helly number;\n   with a declared cut, h=2 on arcs not crossing it. Shannon partitions have no finite Helly number.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L3 — OPEN author statement\n\nExcluding any value from the maximal coincidence may exclude the truth; keeping the fork is the only correct action.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L4 — OPEN author statement\n\nEach entering origin closes bits and spends confidence; the guarantee of the meet is 1 − Σp UNDER DECLARED,\n   JUSTIFIED failure probabilities p_i; if Σp ≥ 1 the bound is trivial and must be reported as such. Agreement\n   and copy count do not estimate p.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L5 — OPEN author statement\n\nIn the Shannon lattice, shared information may have no carrier: at most log₂n − 2 + 2/n bits.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L6 — OPEN author statement\n\nInformation about the truth is bounded by the structure of causes, not by the number of witnesses; copies do not add.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L7 — OPEN author statement\n\nA closed group cannot measure its own reliability: for a cause covering all witnesses, P(unanimity on v) = c/n\n   for every accuracy q, so q is unidentifiable from inside.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L8 — OPEN author statement\n\nOnly dissent identifies what origins share; unanimity says nothing. For a partial cause, q is identified iff an\n   outsider exists with error p ≠ (n−1)/n. Rank-breaking structures: same-set factors, singleton factors,\n   cycle-covering factors, more factors than pairs.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## L9 — OPEN author statement\n\nWhich parameters can be measured is known before observing, from the pairs matrix of declared causes.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## F1 — OPEN author statement\n\nExtremal: over n equiprobable states, max RI(x,y) = log₂n − 2 + 2/n, attained only by the path on n+1 vertices\n   (x groups edges by even endpoint, y by odd). Proof chain: lem-phi (φ(t) ≥ 2(t−1)) → lem-merge → lem-identity →\n   lem-join → lem-meet → thm-extremal. Enumeration n=3..7: 0.251629, 0.500000, 0.721928, 0.918296, 1.093069;\n   pair counts 25, 225, 2704, 41209, 769129 (Bell numbers squared → complete).\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## F2 — OPEN author statement\n\nCircle of 12 points, arcs of length 5 starting at 0, 4, 8: every pair meets, the three do not.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## F3 — OPEN author statement\n\nHalf-plane claims x+y≤12 (seller), x≥3 (buyer), y≥2 (carrier), x+y≥14 (auditor): CONFLICT, witness\n   {seller, auditor}, 2 of 4. Minimal example needing three: x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0, x + y ≤ −1 (pairwise consistent,\n   jointly empty). Both go in as vectors.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## F4 — OPEN author statement\n\nPhase: RI = log₂(n/p) − h(s/p) with n states, period p dividing n, shift s with 0 ≤ s < p, h the binary entropy;\n   worst case is near-phase, not anti-phase. (Author to confirm the domain; until then the vector carries these\n   hypotheses explicitly.)\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## F5 — OPEN author statement\n\nM/4: with a common cause c of accuracy q, C = log₂n − c·[h(q) + (1−q)·log₂(n−1)]; dissent\n   d = (1−c)·[1 − (1−p)² − p²/(n−1)]. Sample n=4, c=1/5: one covering factor q=0 → 1.683 bits; {A,B},{A,B} → 1.430;\n   {A,B},{C,D} → 1.937; triangle {A,B},{B,C},{A,C} → 1.835; q=1/2 → 1.642. Numeric policy: binary64-log2.\n   Negative sample (each a named refusal): missing q → refuse; 2 witnesses requesting c → unmeasured; 3 binary\n   witnesses → unmeasured; perfect agreement → no-dissent; copies → same bound; partial governance → unmeasured.\n   HOW FACTORS GOVERN in duplicated/disjoint/triangle models is NOT fully specified: region stays open (§5).\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P1 — OPEN author statement\n\nObligations: a cell may declare names it needs; an obligation is an open region of form bytes inside the cell\n   (not an edge). Bytes hashing to the name narrow it to a point; received bytes are themselves a cell whose open\n   regions fold inside the parent's. Terminates: the knowledge order is well-founded, plus an instruction budget.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P2 — OPEN author statement\n\nByte regions: open / resolved / fork (two holders, two byte sets: both kept) / unmet (no holder: stop, name it).\n   Wrong bytes are refused, never patched.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P3 — OPEN author statement\n\nNamed core: a result declares the names it depends on; validity is a function of that core only.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P4 — OPEN author statement\n\nRoot as a cell of names: a list of names folds into one name. Atoms (form bytes) have no dissent; dissent lives\n   in claims. The atom zero (fold/hash/assemble) is trusted out of band; in Bound it is the WebAssembly kernel.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P5 — OPEN author statement\n\nName in the fragment: a link carries #form:hash, not a place; the form is in the name because it declares how\n   claims combine (Helly order). Expected addresses: hash(\"answer to claim X\") is known before the answer exists.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P6 — OPEN author statement\n\nPaper as holder: a QR holds a name or small bytes (one QR 2,953 B; A4 sheet ≈140 KB); two tiers of \"belongs to\n   no one\": complete-on-paper, and named (bytes exist while someone keeps them).\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P7 — OPEN author statement\n\nCopresence: commit-reveal; horizon ≥ max latency; decisions with duration; actions as intervals.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P8 — OPEN author statement\n\nFold-as-you-go: resolve by frontier, by need, by proximity.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P9 — OPEN author statement\n\nUniversality test: a primitive enters only if it means the same in a game, a news story and a sensor without\n   code change. Never in a contract: ticks, demos, games, pages, APIs.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## P10 — OPEN author statement\n\nDerived regions: form=derived, value = f(named regions), closing policy eager|deferred (from Scion's derived\n   data; passes P9). Verification is a claim, not a gate: implementation claims fold immediately; verification is\n   a derived region closed later. Cost of folding a cell ∝ the cell, never the world.\n\nSource: docs/theory-2026-10.md; status: proposed/open. Distinguishing vector and hypothesis review remain pending.\n\n## H3 and H5 — proposed experiment relabel\n\nThe retained finite modeled observations have an unsigned experiment relabel proposal. They were already conjectures; this preparation does not call them proven laws or physical results. H5 depends on the H3 experiment and supports four advertised offers (decohere, distinct, sameObject, budget). Re-grounding those offers remains open; the separate retirement lot is a review alternative. No active authority, native rendering or receipt closure is claimed.\n" at=witness:042/theory-source by=target form=alphabet measure=text needs=docs/theory-2026-10.md|docs/theory.lines role=writes scope=prose/en/theory shape=docs/theory.md value=lock
